evals.query:
We are upgrading an old chat server from Socket.IO 2 to Socket.IO 4.8 and the web client from socket.io-client 2 to 4.8. Rewrite this code for v4 and tell me how to roll it out without breaking users who still have the old client cached.

Server:
```js
const io = require('socket.io')(server, { origins: 'https://chat.example.com:*' });
io.set('authorization', (handshake, cb) => cb(null, check(handshake.query.token)));
io.on('connection', (socket) => {
  socket.join('lobby', () => {
    console.log(Object.keys(socket.rooms));
    socket.to('lobby').broadcast.emit('joined', socket.id);
  });
});
```

Client:
```js
const socket = io('https://api.example.com', { query: { token } });
socket.on('error', (err) => showLogin(err));
socket.on('reconnect_attempt', () => console.log('retrying'));
```
